---
import SectionHead from './SectionHead.astro';
---

<section id="about" class="scroll-mt-20 px-5 py-20 sm:px-8 sm:py-28">
  <SectionHead index="01" label="Currently" title="What I do" />

  <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1.2fr_1fr]">
    <div class="space-y-5 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-mute" data-reveal>
      <p>
        I'm a second-year BSc AI (Honours) student
        at <strong class="text-ink font-medium">VU Amsterdam</strong>, doing AI and data
        science at <strong class="text-ink font-medium">Siemens</strong>. I work on
        computer vision, LLM pipelines, and full-stack tools that end up in real hands:
        a Chrome extension used by teachers across VU, an open-source Canvas backup
        tool with 4,000+ users, and an agentic reporting system for a sustainability
        consultancy.
      </p>
      <p>
        On the side I've taught AI workshops to 300+ university faculty and staff, and
        I compete in hackathons: finalist at the Prosus × AISO agent hackathon, and a
        multimodal banking agent built in 24 hours at bunq Hackathon 7.0. If you're
        building something with applied ML, I'd like to hear about it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ul class="voice-mono space-y-0 self-start" data-reveal>
      {
        [
          ['Siemens NL', 'Data science & AI'],
          ['VU Teaching & Learning', 'AI in education'],
          ['AISO', 'AI engineer, platform'],
          ['VU Amsterdam', 'Honours committee'],
        ].map(([org, role]) => (
          <li class="border-line flex flex-wrap justify-between gap-x-6 gap-y-1 border-b border-dashed py-3.5">
            <span class="text-ink">{org}</span>
            <span class="text-mute normal-case tracking-normal">{role}</span>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
